  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "Fixed `normalizeText` in `normalize.mjs`.\n\n**Change made:** Added `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` between `.trim()` and `.toLowerCase()`.\n\n**Why it works:**\n- `typeof value !== 'string'` → throws `TypeError` (unchanged).\n- `.trim()` removes leading/trailing JavaScript whitespace (spaces, tabs, line breaks, etc.).\n- `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` collapses every nonempty internal run of whitespace into a single ASCII space. Since trimming already removed the outer runs, no stray leading/trailing space is introduced.\n- `.toLowerCase()` lowercases all letters via `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`.\n- Empty or whitespace-only input trims to `''`, and the regex finds no matches, so it returns `''`.\n\nThe named export and public tests were left untouched.",
